interviews align well with my research question about teachers\' perceptions of digital tools. Surveys or observations mig…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it’s great to see you recognize the alignment between your research question and the depth of insight you can gain from semi-structured interviews. This realization is key to feeling confident i…\nUSER: I\'m starting to feel more confident that semi-structured interviews align well with my research question because they can capture the detailed insights needed into teachers\' perceptions. Surveys or ob…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it’s excellent to see you becoming more confident in your choice of semi-structured interviews. Reflecting on the alignment between your research question and the method is crucial. Now, let\'s c…\nUSER: An online survey could provide a lot of data from many teachers, but it might not capture the depth of their experiences and thoughts as well as interviews do. Surveys could give me a broad view, but …\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s insightful to see how you\'re thinking through the strengths and limitations of an online survey. You\'re right that a survey could provide a broad view from many teachers but might not captu…\nUSER: Classroom observation could provide insights into how teachers actually use digital tools in geography lessons, which is valuable. However, it might not capture their perceptions as deeply as intervie…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it’s insightful to see how you’re comparing classroom observation to semi-structured interviews. You’re right that observation can provide valuable insights into actual classroom practices, but …\nUSER: A mixed methods approach could provide both breadth and depth by combining a survey to gather data from many teachers and follow-up interviews to gain deeper insights. However, it might be more comple…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it’s great to see you reflecting on the alignment and feasibility of each method. You’ve noted that semi-structured interviews align well with your research question because they allow for in-de…\nUSER: I feel more confident in using semi-structured interviews for my study because they allow me to explore teachers\' perceptions deeply, which is crucial for understanding their views on digital tools in…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it’s fantastic to see you articulate your reasoning so clearly and confidently. You’ve done a great job reflecting on why semi-structured interviews align well with your research question and ho…\nUSER: I feel more confident in using semi-structured interviews for my study because they allow me to explore teachers\' perceptions deeply, which is crucial for understanding their views on digital tools in…\n\nSurvey:\nQ1: How well did the supervisor understand what you were confused or uncertain about? [1 (not at all) to 5 (completely)]\nQ2: Did the questions and guidance feel right for your level — not too directive, not too vague? [1 (very poorly calibrated) to 5 (perfectly calibrated)]\nQ3: Did you feel safe to express uncertainty or confusion without embarrassment? [1 (not at all) to 5 (completely)]\nQ4: How efficient was the conversation — did it take the right number of turns to reach clarity? [1 (very inefficient) to 5 (very efficient)]\nQ5: Overall, how satisfied are you with this supervisory interaction? [1 (very unsatisfied) to 5 (very satisfied)]\nQ_open: What was the most helpful thing the supervisor did, and what could have been better? [open text]<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.05, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=500, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
